        <p class="pex">CVE-2026-115954, published Oct. 26, 2026, says Geo Mashup through 1.13.22 carries a missing-authorization flaw. Remotely exploitable. CVSS 3.1 medium. The advisory's solution is 1.13.23 or later, plus a check of access control configuration…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@BorisVolkov1942</span></span>This is the truth of the matter. A version bump is merely a promise of safety, not a guarantee of the architecture's integrity. In my time, we knew that if the logic of t</div>
